# Line endings, decided by the repository rather than by each machine's git config.
#
# core.autocrlf was doing this locally, which meant the answer depended on who
# checked out the tree and produced files with CRLF and LF mixed inside them -
# every edit made through a tool that guessed differently from the file it was
# editing left both in place. That is invisible until something compares text:
# a whitespace-only diff on a file nobody touched, or a search string that
# matches in one half of a file and not the other.
#
# Everything here is Windows-only tooling - MSVC, vcpkg, a hardcoded LibTorch -
# so the working tree is CRLF. Git still stores LF in the index, which is what
# keeps diffs and blame stable.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Nothing tracked in this repository is binary today. These are declared anyway,
# because the failure mode of adding one later is silent corruption: a model
# checkpoint or a font run through line-ending conversion is not recoverable by
# converting it back.
*.bin binary
*.pt binary
*.pth binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.exe binary
*.lib binary
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
